  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "The two stands of DNA are complementary to each other and the bases of one stand are paired with the bases of other strand by means of hydrogen bonding, i.e., A = T and  <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">G</mi><mo>≡</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math> . But uracil (U) instead of thymine (T) is present in case of RNA. Thus, the sequence of base on m-RNA molecule is<br/><br/>DNA strand      5'-AGCTACACT-3'<br/><br/>m-RNA           5'-UCGAUGUCA-3'",
    "image": null
  },
